@startuml
!include ../style.iuml
autonumber
title Sequence 5 — Session refresh: rotation with reuse detection

participant "Client\n(web: httpOnly cookie,\nmobile: secure store)" as C
participant "POST /api/auth/session/refresh" as Api
participant "SessionHandler" as H
participant "JwtTokenService" as T
database "SQL Server\n(auth.RefreshTokens)" as Sql

C -> Api : refresh token
Api -> H : RefreshAsync
H -> T : HashRefreshToken (SHA-256)
H -> Sql : find token by hash
alt unknown or expired
  H --> C : 401 session_expired
else rotated more than 10 s ago (a copy is being replayed)
  H -> Sql : revoke the whole family (ReuseDetected)
  H --> C : 401 session_expired — thief and user must both sign in
else rotated within 10 s (two tabs refreshed at once)
  H --> C : 409 session_superseded — the family survives
end
H -> Sql : user Active? SecurityStamp unchanged?
alt suspended, deleted, password changed, "log out everywhere"
  H -> Sql : revoke the family
  H --> C : 401 session_expired
end
H -> Sql : the user's institutions (memberships re-checked,\na revoked role drops out of the new token)
H -> T : Issue(UserId, active InstitutionId, IsPlatform)
H -> Sql : BEGIN TRANSACTION
H -> Sql : UPDATE RefreshTokens SET RevokedAt = now, RevokedReason = 'Rotated'\nWHERE Id = @id AND RevokedAt IS NULL
alt 0 rows (another request rotated it first)
  H --> C : 409 session_superseded
end
H -> Sql : INSERT successor (same FamilyId, SecurityStamp)
H -> Sql : old.ReplacedByTokenId = successor.Id
H -> Sql : COMMIT
opt request also showed its access token (same user)
  H -> H : carry the step-up grant to the new access token
end
H --> Api : tokens + institutions
Api --> C : 200, new access JWT,\nnew refresh token (cookie scoped to /api/auth/session)

note over C, Sql
  Every dead session gets the same 401 answer,
  so a replayed copy learns nothing about why it failed.
end note
@enduml
